{"id": "EUVD-2026-103790", "enisaUuid": "7eda2ab0-2db7-3a75-9199-73ab7e709bf2", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/packet: prevent TX_RING byte count overflow\n\ntpacket_snd() drains every SEND_REQUEST frame in a TX ring and adds\neach valid packet length to the signed int len_sum. Userspace can\nrecycle completed frames concurrently, so a single blocking send call\nis not bounded by the ring size.\n\nAfter enough successful transmissions len_sum wraps into the negative\nrange. In particular, 65536 65535-byte frames followed by a 65007-byte\nframe produce 0xfffffdef, or -EIOCBQUEUED. sock_sendmsg_nosec() treats\nthat as an impossible return and triggers a BUG. On systems configured\nto panic on oops, a CAP_NET_RAW holder can panic the host kernel.\n\nStop before the next frame would make the byte count exceed INT_MAX.\nThe positive short count leaves that frame pending for a later send\ncall.\n\nA two-thread TPACKET_V2 reproducer triggered the BUG on an arm64 build\nof Linux 7.3-rc4. With this change, the same reproducer returned the\nexpected positive short count without an oops.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:50:50", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:57:29", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ae169d318d5d23bac76ece90a7e2b5cb760ed043", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/be12b221c0301111eeb023be04add3c6ad7c21fe", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/69ca64bbb528898916f309552053c32a04a36ebc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9fd63d284e251332f4874ef9023cde472f315f86", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2cf81fc9505b148b1b70068303ea6ea4b1212403"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98850", "GHSA-prpm-w567-3rvc"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "055125aa-fff4-3f4d-938b-82c78bc80050", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "69e3c75f4d541a6eb151b3ef91f34033cb3ad6e1 <ae169d318d5d23bac76ece90a7e2b5cb760ed043"}, {"id": "16a950e2-da5e-31c7-b865-b2024e43e5f4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "69e3c75f4d541a6eb151b3ef91f34033cb3ad6e1 <be12b221c0301111eeb023be04add3c6ad7c21fe"}, {"id": "2921b652-7674-31ab-af9d-6f72eae73ec4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "5f822865-ba6e-3afe-b678-ace6a6ad6e4c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "69e3c75f4d541a6eb151b3ef91f34033cb3ad6e1 <9fd63d284e251332f4874ef9023cde472f315f86"}, {"id": "961d76c4-2ac9-3149-8c6b-50130b795b60", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "a8d1c3b0-edb6-37c4-ab7d-b6e7a7eee990", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "69e3c75f4d541a6eb151b3ef91f34033cb3ad6e1 <2cf81fc9505b148b1b70068303ea6ea4b1212403"}, {"id": "ad40d434-c39e-3414-9d2f-41ac8cceb72a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "d154d62f-77c3-3dea-9e2e-eac046d2cf97", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "e5f4be29-ac9e-3932-b710-8ade120746f8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.31"}, {"id": "efd7b734-1758-334b-90a0-d0682be72b1a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "69e3c75f4d541a6eb151b3ef91f34033cb3ad6e1 <69ca64bbb528898916f309552053c32a04a36ebc"}, {"id": "ff37c376-d2c7-3c4e-b62f-da51a5ded0db", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "ffe5c88c-8c97-3a14-b234-8fc5ab9fc0e8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "ab310e75-b16e-31ce-b61f-a5a066a6ffa8", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}